In freediving we have to deal with a specific, stressful and unusual set of challenges and conditions.\
\
Here are five hallmarks of the freediving experience\
\
1) Presense\
\
Freedivers interviewed for this study all reported experiencing an \'93unusual state of heightened presence, or situated focus and awareness of the current moment\'94. \
\
2) Perception\
\
Freedivers seem to have a sense of heightened interoception (sensing the internal state of our bodies) and exteroception (perceiving stimuli originating outside the body).\
\
3) Reflection\
\
We are more pre-reflective, meaning that our experience is \'91lived through as the subject of awareness, without any process of reflection on itself\'92 \'94, with a feeling of being \'93choicelessly aware\'94 if you will.\
\
4) Decision making\
\
Although we are in an ever shifting environment and each dive is different than the one before it - something that should in theory pose a heavy cognitive load on us - it appears that very little effort is used to make the decisions we need to make while diving. \
\
5) Emotion\
\
In some ways, during a dive our emotions undergo a quieting down, we have a more restricted range and they manifest to a lesser degree. \
\
The Skilled Intentionality Framework\
\
The SIF is a conceptual framework which brings together insights from various sciences in order to investigate cognition in skilled action.\
\
Some key concepts are \'93affordances\'94 (possibilities for action informed by our needs), action-readiness (a bodily state of readiness for a specific action) and the \'93metastable zone\'94 (an equilibrium where we are open to changes and to act flexibly).\
\
Freediving represents a unique \'93ultra-flexible\'94 state since it requires an optimal and truly exceptional balancing, or attunement, of crucial internal and external conditions.\
\
One area where freediving and the SI Framework diverge is anticipation, it being a key tenet of skilled action in SIF but something that freedivers lack during the dive. \
\
For a more in-depth analysis and to read the full article, head over to the Blog section of my website (link on my profile).\
